es","\u002Fen\u002Freleases","en\u002F5.releases",[273],{"title":274,"icon":12,"path":275,"stem":276,"children":277,"page":12},"Versions","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions",[278,282,286,290,294],{"title":279,"path":280,"stem":281},"v3.2.2","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-2-2","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F1.v3-2-2",{"title":283,"path":284,"stem":285},"v3.2.1","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-2-1","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F2.v3-2-1",{"title":287,"path":288,"stem":289},"v3.2.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-2-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F3.v3-2-0",{"title":291,"path":292,"stem":293},"v3.1.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-1-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F4.v3-1-0",{"title":295,"path":296,"stem":297},"v3.0.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-0-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F5.v3-0-0",{"id":299,"title":117,"body":300,"description":1244,"extension":1245,"links":1246,"meta":1251,"navigation":1252,"path":118,"seo":1253,"stem":119,"__hash__":1254},"docs_en\u002Fen\u002F3.components\u002F2.text\u002F2.input-number.md",{"type":301,"value":302,"toc":1219},"minimark",[303,311,316,321,344,348,399,403,437,440,576,601,623,627,639,642,661,665,681,684,687,694,697,701,708,711,715,718,734,737,741,748,751,755,775,778,782,795,798,802,809,812,816,820,845,848,924,929,933,970,974,1011,1143,1187,1212,1216],[304,305,306,310],"p",{},[307,308,309],"code",{},"v-model: number | null",".",[312,313,315],"h2",{"id":314},"usage","Usage",[317,318,320],"h3",{"id":319},"decimal-places-and-thousands-separators","Decimal places and thousands separators",[304,322,323,326,327,330,331,334,335,326,338,340,341,343],{},[307,324,325],{},"decimal"," defaults to ",[307,328,329],{},"false",", allowing only integers; a positive integer sets the number of decimal places, and ",[307,332,333],{},"true"," allows any number. ",[307,336,337],{},"thousand-separator",[307,339,333],{},", showing thousands separators on blur; pass ",[307,342,329],{}," for numbers such as years or codes that should not have them.",[345,346],"component-example",{"name":347},"input-number-decimal",[349,350,351,366,379],"ul",{},[352,353,354,355,358,359,362,363,365],"li",{},"While typing, the sign, decimal point and trailing zeros are kept; incomplete input (such as just ",[307,356,357],{},"-",") binds ",[307,360,361],{},"null",". On blur, the value is rounded and padded according to ",[307,364,325],{},", and thousands separators are shown.",[352,367,368,369,371,372,374,375,378],{},"Non-numeric characters and decimals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[307,370,325],{}," is ",[307,373,329],{}," or ",[307,376,377],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[352,380,381,382,371,385,388,389,371,391,374,393,395,396,398],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[307,383,384],{},"inputmode",[307,386,387],{},"numeric"," when ",[307,390,325],{},[307,392,329],{},[307,394,377],{},", and ",[307,397,325],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[317,400,402],{"id":401},"step-buttons","Step buttons",[304,404,405,408,409,412,413,416,417,420,421,424,425,428,429,432,433,436],{},[307,406,407],{},"buttons"," shows increment and decrement buttons (off by default), ",[307,410,411],{},"step"," is the amount per step (",[307,414,415],{},"1"," by default), and ",[307,418,419],{},"min",", ",[307,422,423],{},"max"," limit stepping with the buttons and keys. ",[307,426,427],{},"orientation"," sets the button layout: ",[307,430,431],{},"horizontal"," (default) puts decrement on the left and increment on the right and centers the number; ",[307,434,435],{},"vertical"," stacks both on the right and keeps the number right-aligned.",[345,438],{"name":439},"input-number-step",[349,441,442,465,471,488,504,547,559,566],{},[352,443,444,448,449,451,452,420,454,420,456,458,459,461,462,464],{},[445,446,447],"strong",{},"Keyboard",": with ",[307,450,407],{},", or when any of ",[307,453,411],{},[307,455,419],{},[307,457,423],{}," is passed, ArrowUp \u002F ArrowDown steps once in the focused input, PageUp \u002F PageDown steps 10 times, and Home \u002F End jump to ",[307,460,419],{}," \u002F ",[307,463,423],{}," (when set). Without these settings the arrow keys behave as in a normal text input. The buttons are not in the Tab order and are labelled \"Increment\" and \"Decrement\" (following the locale).",[352,466,467,470],{},[445,468,469],{},"Press and hold",": holding a button for more than 0.4 seconds keeps stepping until a limit is reached or the button is released. Pressing a button does not move focus away from the input.",[352,472,473,476,477,479,480,482,483,485,486,310],{},[445,474,475],{},"Empty value",": when the value is ",[307,478,361],{},", both increment and decrement start at ",[307,481,419],{},", or at ",[307,484,377],{}," without ",[307,487,419],{},[352,489,490,493,494,497,498,501,502,310],{},[445,491,492],{},"No floating-point errors",": steps are computed in decimal, so repeatedly adding ",[307,495,496],{},"0.25"," never gives ",[307,499,500],{},"0.7500000001","; the result is rounded to the places allowed by ",[307,503,325],{},[352,505,506,513,514,516,517,519,520,522,523,525,526,528,529,531,532,534,535,537,538,540,541,543,544,546],{},[445,507,508,510,511],{},[307,509,411],{}," and ",[307,512,325],{},": when ",[307,515,411],{}," has more decimal places than ",[307,518,325],{}," allows (for example ",[307,521,496],{}," with ",[307,524,325],{}," set to ",[307,527,329],{},"), the step is rounded to what ",[307,530,325],{}," allows (at least one smallest unit, ",[307,533,415],{}," for ",[307,536,329],{},") with a console warning. A ",[307,539,411],{}," that is not a number above 0, or a ",[307,542,419],{}," greater than ",[307,545,423],{},", is also ignored with a warning.",[352,548,549,552,553,555,556,558],{},[445,550,551],{},"Limits",": the increment button is disabled when the value is at or above ",[307,554,423],{},", and the decrement button at or below ",[307,557,419],{},". Both are disabled while disabled, loading, in a skeleton or in a disabled form.",[352,560,561,562,565],{},"Each step triggers the ",[307,563,564],{},"UFormField"," input and change validation, just like typing.",[352,567,568,510,570,572,573,310],{},[307,569,407],{},[307,571,427],{}," can have site-wide defaults, for example to show the buttons across the project: ",[307,574,575],{},"shuoUi.components.inputNumber.buttons: true",[577,578,579,510,581,583,584,587,588,510,591,594,595,600],"warning",{},[307,580,419],{},[307,582,423],{}," only limit the buttons and keys. ",[445,585,586],{},"A typed value outside the range is not corrected","; the bound value stays as typed, and stepping from it moves back into the range. Keep validating the range in the schema with ",[307,589,590],{},"v.minValue",[307,592,593],{},"v.maxValue","; see ",[596,597,599],"a",{"href":598},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[304,602,603,604,461,607,610,611,614,615,618,619,622],{},"In horizontal layout the decrement button takes the place of the left ",[307,605,606],{},"icon",[307,608,609],{},"leadingIcon"," (the ",[307,612,613],{},"#leading"," slot still follows the button); use ",[307,616,617],{},"orientation=\"vertical\""," when you need a left icon. The increment button sits to the right of the unit, the ",[307,620,621],{},"#trailing"," slot and the loading icon, and the padding on both sides follows their actual width, so the number and unit are never pushed out.",[317,624,626],{"id":625},"unit","Unit",[304,628,629,630,371,632,634,635,638],{},"When ",[307,631,625],{},[307,633,333],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[596,636,47],{"href":637},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[345,640],{"name":641},"input-number-unit",[304,643,644,510,646,648,649,653,654,656,657,461,659,310],{},[307,645,625],{},[307,647,337],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[596,650,652],{"href":651},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[307,655,625],{}," only accepts ",[307,658,333],{},[307,660,329],{},[317,662,664],{"id":663},"variants","Variants",[304,666,667,668,420,671,510,674,677,678,310],{},"Uses the ",[307,669,670],{},"variant",[307,672,673],{},"color",[307,675,676],{},"highlight"," of ",[307,679,680],{},"UInput",[345,682],{"name":683},"input-number-variant",[317,685,686],{"id":606},"Icon",[304,688,667,689,677,691,693],{},[307,690,606],{},[307,692,680],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[345,695],{"name":696},"input-number-icon",[317,698,700],{"id":699},"size-and-states","Size and states",[304,702,703,704,707],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[596,705,102],{"href":706},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[345,709],{"name":710},"input-number-states",[312,712,714],{"id":713},"examples","Examples",[317,716,599],{"id":717},"with-form-validation",[304,719,720,721,724,725,510,727,729,730,733],{},"Use ",[307,722,723],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[307,726,590],{},[307,728,593],{},"; use ",[307,731,732],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[345,735],{"name":736},"input-number-validation",[317,738,740],{"id":739},"step-buttons-with-validation","Step buttons with validation",[304,742,743,510,745,747],{},[307,744,419],{},[307,746,423],{}," do not replace validation: the buttons in this examp